{
  "Pages side by side, one in sight: a swipe or a drag brings the next one, and so do `next()`, `previous()` and `goTo()`, or a [Tabs](/tabs), a [Stepper](/stepper) or buttons bound to the same value. The panels of a tab strip without the strip.": "",
  "Pages driven by a stepper": "",
  "The `View` children are the pages; the one in sight is `value` (a view’s `key`, else its index), `x-model` binds it two-way. Here a `Stepper` shares the value: a press on a step and a swipe on a page move both. A page is built when first in sight (`lazy`).": "",
  "Built when first in sight, kept or not": "",
  "`lazy` (the default) builds a view when it first comes into sight and keeps it; `keepAlive={false}` disposes what a view’s `content` made while it is out of sight, and makes it again the next time. The JSX children stay either way, as in `Tabs`.": "",
  "Made with `new`, views added with `add()` and `insert()`, removed with `remove()`; `loop` goes around the ends, `animated={false}` shows the next view at once.": "",
  "A `group` named “Pages” in the kit language; several on one page: give each its own `label`.": "",
  "A `group` named by its `title`, else “Page 2 of 3”; the views out of sight are hidden from readers and from the keys (`inert`), so Tab moves only inside the view in sight.": "",
  "A swipe needs a finger or a mouse: give the keys a way too, a `Tabs`, a `Stepper` or buttons bound to the same `value`, as the examples do.": "",
  "The multi-view. `data-swipe` when a drag moves it, `data-dragging` while one does, `data-still` with `animated` off.": "",
  "The frame that clips the views and the track that slides in it (`data-dragging`, `data-no-motion`).": "",
  "A view (`aria-hidden`, `inert` out of sight).": "",
  "Units: the frame (`swipeable`, `dragging`) and a view.": "",
  "Between the views, seen while a finger drags them.": "",
  "MultiView props": "",
  "The view in sight: its `key`, else its index. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "After the last view comes the first; the move goes around the ends, not back across the views between.": "",
  "A finger or a pointer drags the views; a drag far or fast enough lands on the next one.": "",
  "The views slide into sight. `false` shows the next one at once.": "",
  "A view is built when first in sight, then kept (a view’s own `lazy` wins).": "",
  "`false` disposes what a view’s `content` made while the view is out of sight (a view’s own `keepAlive` wins).": "",
  "View props": "",
  "“Page 2 of 3”": "",
  "What screen readers call the view.": "",
  "Names the view in `value`; the JSX `key` is read too.": "",
  "Content made when the view is first in sight, besides the JSX children.": "",
  "The view’s own settings; `undefined` follows the multi-view.": "",
  "A hidden view takes no room and is skipped; a disabled one is skipped by `next()` and `previous()` and refused by `goTo()`.": "",
  "The view in sight is about to change (`from`, `to`, `fromView`, `toView`, `byUser`); `cancel = true` keeps the one there.": "",
  "The view in sight changed (`index`, `view`, `previous`, `byUser`: by a swipe, else programmatically).": "",
  "The views in order, hidden ones too.": "",
  "The view in sight and its index; `null` and -1 when there is none.": "",
  "How many views there are.": "",
  "Goes to the next or the previous view that is shown and enabled; `false` at an end without `loop`, or when refused.": "",
  "Goes to a view, by index, key or the `View` itself; `onSelecting` is asked first. A view’s own `select()` does the same.": "",
  "Adds a view at the end or at an index; one from another multi-view moves here.": "",
  "Removes a view and disposes it; the sight moves to a neighbour.": ""
}
